# Code used for complex non-orthogonal building handling; generating conformal geometry and applying it the the application of mesh generation
This directory contains most of the code used in the following publication:

Ezendam, T., van der, Hofmeyer, H., van der Wal, S., Perevendieva K.G., and Emmerich, M. T. M. "Handling Complex Building Geometries for Disciplinary Processing in Conceptual Building Design Simulation and Optimization". In: Computing in Civil Engineering (2026). DOI: 10.1061/JCCEE5.CPENG-6922 

The remaining used code for this publication can be found at:
- For the mesh convergence study comparing all three methods:
    - Tying method convergence study source code and data: 
      Ezendam, T., van der Wal, S., & Hofmeyer, H. (2026). BSO Toolbox: Tying method (Version 1.0.0) [Computer software]. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23476925
    - IP method convergence study source code and data: 
      Ezendam, T., & Hofmeyer, H. BSO Toolbox (Version 1.0.0) [Computer software]. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23477078

The following code is included in this directory:

* an executable to test the IP and TP method on their effectiveness of generating a conformal geometry (~/Complex_NOBSD_handeling/Effectiveness_conformal_making)
* an executable 
* an executable to compare the mesh quality of the IP and TP method with the benchmark case (~/Complex_NOBSD_handling/Mesh_Quality_study_IP_TP_methods)

Furthermore the following supplementary data is supplied:

* the building spatial designs used for the each of the case studies (All orthogonal designs are included in the executa~/Complex_NOBSD_handeling/Effectiveness_conformal_making)
* the settings (structural and thermal design) used for the case studies
* data_files for 
